{"id":"Prowl.Runtime.TextMeshComponent","name":"TextMeshComponent","display":"TextMeshComponent","kind":"class","assembly":"Prowl.Runtime","namespace":"Prowl.Runtime","outer":null,"signature":"public class TextMeshComponent : Component, IMaterialRenderer, IColorTint, IRenderSync","bases":[{"name":"Component","id":"Prowl.Runtime.Component"},{"name":"IMaterialRenderer","id":"Prowl.Runtime.IMaterialRenderer"},{"name":"IColorTint","id":"Prowl.Runtime.IColorTint"},{"name":"IRenderSync","id":"Prowl.Runtime.Rendering.IRenderSync"}],"docs":{"summary":"Draws text as a mesh in arbitrary 3D world space, independent of any [`GameCanvas`](#api~Prowl.Runtime.GameCanvas). The glyph geometry is generated once by Scribe (shared atlas via `UIFontSystem`), baked into a cached [`Mesh`](#api~Prowl.Runtime.Resources.Mesh), and drawn through the `Default/DefaultTextMesh` SDF shader - so it stays crisp at any distance without the per-frame cost of a canvas. The text is anchored around the transform origin (see [`Anchor`](#api~Prowl.Runtime.TextMeshComponent~Anchor)), so a centered anchor puts the middle of the text on the object's position. To make a camera-facing nameplate, rotate the transform to face the camera yourself (billboard); nothing here forces an orientation."},"attributes":["AddComponentMenu","ComponentIcon"],"members":[{"kind":"property","name":"Font","signature":"public FontAsset? Font { get; set; }","docs":{},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":42,"path":"Prowl.Runtime/Components/TextMeshComponent.cs","anchor":"Font"},{"kind":"property","name":"ResolvedFont","signature":"public FontAsset? ResolvedFont { get; }","docs":{"summary":"The assigned font, or the engine's embedded default font when none is set."},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":45,"path":"Prowl.Runtime/Components/TextMeshComponent.cs","anchor":"ResolvedFont"},{"kind":"property","name":"Text","signature":"public string Text { get; set; }","docs":{},"static":false,"obsolete":false,"line":55,"path":"Prowl.Ru